@.str.36 = private unnamed_addr constant [871 x i8] c"\0A          Maximum number of jobs that Nix will try to build locally in parallel.\0A\0A          The special value `auto` causes Nix to use the number of CPUs in your system.\0A          Use `0` to disable local builds and directly use the remote machines specified in [`builders`](#conf-builders).\0A          This will not affect derivations that have [`preferLocalBuild = true`](@docroot@/language/advanced-attributes.md#adv-attr-preferLocalBuild), which are always built locally.\0A\0A          > **Note**\0A          >\0A          > The number of CPU cores to use for each build job is independently determined by the [`cores`](#conf-cores) setting.\0A\0A          <!-- TODO(@fricklerhandwerk): would be good to have those shorthands for common options as part of the specification -->\0A          The setting can be overridden using the `--max-jobs` (`-j`) command line switch.\0A        \00", align 1
